        <p>Week's contribution to 20th Novem- ber, 1914 Amount previously acknowledged</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-11-21_WidnesExaminer_art0147" n="art0147">
        <head>FURNITURE</head>
        <p>FURNITURE</p>
        <p>- RN-lands and Mrs. Tho•di sot. PROVISIONS.—Mr. Kitchen. Mr. F. Lindley., Mr. James Bate. Mrs. Seeker, Mr. W. :Mcln- tyre, Miss Warren, Col. Lyon, Mr. Miller, and . Mr. Wm. Monks.</p>
        <p>NUNNERLEY HOUSE. FURNITURE, &amp;c.—Mrs. Spinks, 4, Salisbury- street; Mrs. Bostock, Mrs. Bedell, Wilcock cl Sadler, Mrs. Bracecamp, Mrs. Carleton, Miss Lee, Mrs. Bowman, J. &amp; W. Dutton, Mrs. W. P. Rvlands, Mrs. Armitage, Walton Lea; Mrs. Gill, Wilson-Patten-street; Miss Gill, 123, Wilderspool-road ; Mr. Place, Mr. Hill, Mr. Hickman, Mrs. Frost, Grappenhall; Mrs. Naden. Mrs. 17nsworth, Mrs. Fulton-Smith. Mrs. Frost, Mr. Lowe, Mrs. James Bowcock-, Mrs. John Evans, Mr. Garland, Mrs. Braide, Mrs. Bell, Mrs. Wilson, Mrs. J. J. Sanders)n, Fletcher, Russell &amp; Co., Ltd., Mrs. Liston. Mrs. Harrison, Mrs. Fox, Mrs. Robson Chor- ley, Mrs. O'Brien. Mrs. Maginn, Mr. Hick- man, and Misses White.</p>
        <p>CIOUNTV BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON. NJ TOBACCO FUND FOR THE 21,m SOUTH LANCASHIRES (THE WARRINGTON LINE BATTALION) SERVING AT THE FRONT. s. d. J. B. Storey • 2 2 0 Mrs. T. Locker and Mrs. F. Lindley 2 0 0 Collection " Constitution" Lodge, In- dependent Order of Oddfellows, M.U 1 2 0 Nemo Fund Pupils Secondary School Proceeds of Draw, per Mrs. Tomkin- son, Wellfield-street Staff T. &amp; W. Dutton, 4th con 0 10 6 Garment Room, Castle Rubber Works, 2nd con. Mrs. E. Atkinson</p>
