      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-11-21_WidnesExaminer_art0177" n="art0177">
        <head>HIGH LEGO.</head>
        <p>HIGH LEGO.</p>
        <p>The Price of Obscenity..—At the L9lll,l—ii Sessions on Wednesday morning, Simpson, a labourer, of Ditchfield's-lane, Legh, was summoned for using ()Welled guage.—P.C. Gould' proved the case, 811,. fendant, who did not appear, but seated by his mother, was fined ss.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1914-11-21_WidnesExaminer_art0178" n="art0178">
        <head>WIN WICK.</head>
        <p>WIN WICK.</p>
        <p>To Help the, Retie" Funds.—A meeting2tssl ishioners was held in the schoolroom on 111°-,.sio evening, the object being to endeavour to 'tiler money for the Prince of Wales' ancimr°lned' Relief Fund's. A strong committee aton• consisting of the following: Messrs. P. l'„°'Wol" A. Alker, J. Shaw, R. Hambleten' W. lace, C. Gerosa, P. E. Dutton, J. E retv- Swee F. Uncles, F. •• Collins, M. Mearne and • .fter' love. A meeting of the committee Was 1,-ose: wards had, and it was decided to make a till to-house collection. It was also suggesteu s tbe sacseries of concerts might be held as soon fl schools which are being enlarged, are g able.</p>
        <p>Got There! ore "Five hundred German prisoneltd cor landed in Dublin yesterday afternoon 3'ooo veyed under escort to Templemore,A Tipperary."—" Newcahtle Daily Jour n,.• tber° v "It's a long, long way, but they've o at last."—" Punch."</p>
