        <p>LANCASHIRE INSURANCE COMMITTEE. Any Insured Persons who desire to change their DOCTOR or INSTITUTION, or the method by which they have been obtaining medical treatment, as from the Ist January next, must give notice to the Committee before the Ist DECEMBER next. Such notice should be given by sending to the Committee at 1, FISHERGATE HILL, PRES- TON, before the date named, the MEDICAL CARD, together with a letter signed by the insured person stating his desire to change. HARCOURT E. CLARE, Clerk to the Committee. Preston, 9th November, 1914. _ WARRINGTON INSURANCE COMMITTEE. CHANGE OF DOCTOR. Insured persons desirous of changing their Panel Doctor or Institution at the close of the current year should give notice thereof in writing to the under- mentioned not later than the Ist day of December, 1914. The notice must be accompanied by the Medical Card. Applications received after the Ist December will not be entertained. Dated this 6th day of November, 1914. ALFRED TILLING, Clerk to the Committee. Trinity Chambers, Market Gate, Warrington.</p>
        <p>HE WARRINGTON MUSEUM A- COMMITTEE beg to announce that the following POPULAR LECTURES On "ROME, THE ETERNAL CITY: ITS STORY AND ITS MONUMENTS," Will be delivered by J. E. PHYTHIAN, ESQ. SATURDAY, NOVEMBER 21ST: "Early Christian and Mediawal ROMO." SATURDAY, NOVEMBER 28TH: "Rome of the Renaissance." SATURDAY, DECEMBER sni: "Modern Rome." Lantern Illustrations. At the CO-OPERATIVE HALL, CAIRO-ST., at 7.30 p.m. Admission Free.</p>
        <p>STOCKTON HEATH. "WHY WE WENT TO WAR." AN ILLUSTRATED, NON-PARTY, AND EDUCATIONAL LECTURE On the above Subject will be delivered in THE CHURCH ROOM, ON FRIDAY EVENING NEXT, the 27th NOV., at 7.45, by HENRY LANCASTER, Esq. Chairman: Lieut.-Colonel CHARLES LYON. Patriotic Songs by Messrs. Arthur Greenough and Walter Howard. Accompanist: Mr. Frank Booth. Recitations by the Lecturer. ADMISSION FREE, except to a few Reserved Seats, for which application should be made not later than Thursday next, the 26th November. Tickets, One Shilling each. Collection in aid of the BELGIAN RELIEF FUND Further particulars see Handbills. H. J. WESTBROOK, 45, Whitefield-road: S. ALBINSON, 36, Fairfield-road; Hon. Secretaries.</p>
