        <p>66 I was so badly disfigured by eczelma A that I was ashamed to be seen,!9 says Mrs. R. A. Smith, of 7, Lamb St., Oldham. "It started with a sore on my upper lip. This sore discharged matter which caused other places to break out. My face, chin, and neck were soon covered with big patches of raw, wet sores which turned nearly black. Then the disease spread to my head and caused my hair to come out in handsful. "A doctor told me I had eczema very badly. As his treatment didn't cure me I attended the Manchester Skin Hospital for some time. The eczema, however, was still as bad as ever. I had been suffering three years now and felt thoroughly disheartened. "Having heard a lot about Zam-Buk I got a box from the chemist. Judge of my delight when, after the first few applications, Zam-Buk began to clear away the painful and disfiguring sores. "The diseased skin peeled as I kept on applying Zam-Buk. New healthy tissue then grew over my face and neck, and my scalp was also thoroughly cleansed of disease. My hair has grown again thick and healthy. "I have lived in this district 22 years, and the splendid cure worked by Zam-Buk has astonished my friends." fr• Zani-Ruk has no equal as a safe and sure cure for eczema, ulcers and festering wounds, poisoned sores, piles, ringworm, etc., and for quickly soothing and healing cuts, scratches, bruises, knocks, etc. NOTE.—Zam-Buk Balm is never sold from door to door. Refuse all worthless imitations and substitutes</p>
